usage: janus contract draft [-h] --source-id SOURCE_ID (--from-raw RUN_ID |
                            --from-fixture PATH) [--out OUT]
                            [--environment ENVIRONMENT]
                            [--project-root PROJECT_ROOT] [--include-disabled]

Infer one schema from saved raw artifacts or local fixtures and write a draft
contract. This command does not extract data or write to raw or bronze.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --source-id SOURCE_ID
                        Configured source to plan.
  --from-raw RUN_ID     Read artifacts from this exact previous raw run.
  --from-fixture PATH   Read a local fixture; repeat to combine pages or
                        files.
  --out OUT             Write the draft to a project-local path; an explicit
                        path may be replaced.
  --environment ENVIRONMENT
                        Environment profile name under conf/environments
                        without the .yaml suffix.
  --project-root PROJECT_ROOT
                        Project root used to resolve conf/ and data/ paths.
  --include-disabled    Allow planning a configured source that is disabled.

Inference reflects only the supplied artifacts. All-null fields and text
sentinels such as 'N/A' can change inferred types; review a draft before
activating it.
